Subject: [PATCH 088/161] hjviewer: review fixes, core1 lane (1.9)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TV-W2: the unverified-name check also drops the Hangul fillers
(U+115F, U+1160, U+3164, U+FFA0, which NFKC leaves as U+1160 or U+115F
and which show as a blank), so "같은ㅤ계정" and "Sameﾠaccount"
are marked; the shown name loses them too, plus U+061C, U+180E and
U+2060-2064.

TV-C6: the deep-link pins use the keys.rs constants; the pin test keeps
only the assertions that fail without the pins.

TV-W6: the support mark is logged once per connection, when it first
holds it, instead of on every LoginRequest the peer sends; the support
grant's test is appended at the end of hjviewer_access/tests.rs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
